                'about_en' => 'Nasr City is one of Cairo\'s largest, most densely populated, and vibrant districts, established in the 1960s as a modern architectural extension to the capital. It serves as the commercial and business nerve center in the eastern region, characterized by its wide, geometrically organized intersecting streets such as Makram Ebeid, Abbas El Akkad, and Moustafa El Nahhas. The area provides all types of services and houses important government institutions and massive shopping malls, most famously "Citystars". The real estate sector in Nasr City is highly diverse, experiencing robust activity in the sale and rental of residential apartments, as well as commercial and administrative spaces for businesses and clinics.',
